.TH FTELL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ftell \- get a Crunch stream's current position
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "long ftell(struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR ftell ()
returns the current byte position in an unbuffered stream.
It does not change the stream's position or its end-of-file and error indicators.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the current position, or \-1 with
.B errno
set on failure. A null stream fails with
.BR EINVAL ;
a nonseekable stream can fail with
.BR ESPIPE .
Success leaves
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH NOTES
Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fseek (3crunch),
.BR rewind (3crunch),
.BR lseek (3crunch)
